                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "f369a4ca-549b-3db9-81c8-2884c91314f3",
                        "entry_id": "40dd5f97-b8b6-39bb-8dfc-052cb615491f",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Qui pense, qui est capable de penser."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "2d027aa1-7d11-4073-b3c7-89ccb48442f0",
                                "sense_id": "f369a4ca-549b-3db9-81c8-2884c91314f3",
                                "text": "— C’est horrible ! horrible, murmura-t-il, nous sommes indignes de l’humanité… Que ce soit la lâcheté ou l’amour qui ait paralysé Jacques, nous ne devions pas, nous, des natures pensantes, nous laisser aller ainsi à l’emportement."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2ba3cf17-9011-495e-adb0-de7302795f38",
                                "sense_id": "f369a4ca-549b-3db9-81c8-2884c91314f3",
                                "text": "Nous considérons alors que les relations intersubjectives sont indispensables au retour dans la vie du sujet « chosifié » par le traumatisme, et que c’est par la restauration des liens interpersonnels que celui-ci retrouvera sa place au sein de la communauté des êtres vivants en étant repositionné comme être parlant et pensant."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5024d383-d35f-4f2d-8844-891f30a8eb99",
                                "sense_id": "f369a4ca-549b-3db9-81c8-2884c91314f3",
                                "text": "La faculté pensante."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "e0efe649-4064-41ed-9a1d-d73ac20b5cab",
                        "source_entry_id": "40dd5f97-b8b6-39bb-8dfc-052cb615491f",
                        "source_sense_id": "f369a4ca-549b-3db9-81c8-2884c91314f3",
                        "target_lang_word": "thinking",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "thinking",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "46641358-fdb8-357a-b185-754c0ecffb4b",
                                        "entry_id": "75c0bf5b-d84c-3f8f-9d0d-6817c16987ef",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Thought; gerund of think."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b10c90d7-eadd-4a10-be8a-4536bc656ee8",
                                                "sense_id": "46641358-fdb8-357a-b185-754c0ecffb4b",
                                                "text": "What is your thinking on this subject?"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3dda3e28-1fab-49ea-9bfd-388b8db04fe0",
                                                "sense_id": "46641358-fdb8-357a-b185-754c0ecffb4b",
                                                "text": "But how the neurons are organised in these lobes and ganglia remains obscure. Yet this is the level of organisation that does the actual thinking—and is, presumably, the seat of consciousness."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "366654e1-e905-4341-9eb4-dd985d23285d",
                                                "sense_id": "46641358-fdb8-357a-b185-754c0ecffb4b",
                                                "text": "When BR \"back-checked\" (BR's term) the financial results of steam replacement across 49 schemes, where DMUs had been substituted on the London Midland Region, only one was now profitable. BR thinking on such substitutions referred to \"betterment\", not profit or loss."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "thinking",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "46858d80-b480-3dd1-8f86-f5af0e7ea295",
                                        "entry_id": "a15c4c95-47f2-3cd8-a0e0-64d57b28c6d7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "present participle and gerund of think"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "form-of",
                                            "gerund",
                                            "participle",
                                            "present"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1b03287b-bf63-4ba6-96e9-60ea25dc952b",
                                                "sense_id": "46858d80-b480-3dd1-8f86-f5af0e7ea295",
                                                "text": "I'm thinking about inventing a new perpetual-motion machine."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ae28c82c-d390-43e5-9a18-f7b6b3bfc324",
                                                "sense_id": "46858d80-b480-3dd1-8f86-f5af0e7ea295",
                                                "text": "He was thinking; but the glory of the song, the swell from the great organ, the clustered lights, […], the height and vastness of this noble fane, its antiquity and its strength—all these things seemed to have their part as causes of the thrilling emotion that accompanied his thoughts."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "13898bd2-418d-4b76-9c2c-41c57796c2d8",
                        "source_entry_id": "40dd5f97-b8b6-39bb-8dfc-052cb615491f",
